            "rawHtml": "<h3>© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">Virtualization and Cloud Computing Cloud-Based Technology</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>Cloud-based technologies enable organizations like @Apollo to access computing, storage, software and servers through the Internet. It moves the technology component from the organization to the cloud provider. Let&#x27;s recap from Module 1 the three main computing service models, which are collectively known as XaaS (‗anything as a service&#x27;). 1. Software as a Service (SaaS) allows users to access application software and databases. Cloud providers manage the infrastructure while users store data on the cloud provider&#x27;s servers. Ex. Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, and Salesforce 1. Platform as a Service (PaaS) lets an organization remotely access the development tools and services used to deliver such applications, on a subscription basis. Ex. Google App Engine, AWS Elastic Beanstalk, and Microsoft Azure App Service 2. Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) provides virtualized computing resources over the Internet. The provider hosts the hardware, software, servers, and storage components, and the user pays for a subscription to use these resources. Ex. servers (e.g., AWS EC2, Azure VMs, Google Compute Engine), storage, and networking. 8</p></div>",
