            "cleanText": "© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential Cloud Data Security States of Data The States of Data Domain describes controls related to securing the data itself, of which encryption and hashing are of the most important. Customer data should be protected in the following three states: - Data at rest: This refers to data that is in storage. - Data is in this state when no user or process is accessing, requesting, or amending it. - Data at rest can be stored on local devices such as a hard disk in a computer, or a centralized network, such as an organization's server. - In cloud computing, data at rest can be stored in a cloud and is accessible from any computer connected to the internet, usually with subscription. - All data that is not in transit nor in process is considered data at rest. 48",
