            "subtitle": "DevSecOps Principles, CALMS & Secure SDLC",
            "lead": "© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential The CALMS framework is an essential basis for DevOps. Jez Humble and his peers originally proposed it, which applies also",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">The CALMS framework is an essential basis for DevOps. Jez Humble and his peers originally proposed it, which applies also to DevSecOps.</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p> Culture - is what underpins everything around DevOps. It&#x27;s about inclusion, having a safe environment, and a collaborative organization without siloed walls, having a safe environment where people can question, test, and innovate around security.  Automation - the automation of security in testing and delivering monitoring systems through observability. This is essential and one of the more straightforward elements to implement, but it must be done in tandem with all other elements. The CALMS Method</p></div>",
            "cleanText": "© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential The CALMS framework is an essential basis for DevOps. Jez Humble and his peers originally proposed it, which applies also to DevSecOps.  Culture - is what underpins everything around DevOps. It's about inclusion, having a safe environment, and a collaborative organization without siloed walls, having a safe environment where people can question, test, and innovate around security.  Automation - the automation of security in testing and delivering monitoring systems through observability. This is essential and one of the more straightforward elements to implement, but it must be done in tandem with all other elements. The CALMS Method",
