            "subtitle": "DevSecOps Principles, CALMS & Secure SDLC",
            "lead": "© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential The CALMS framework can be effectively applied to DevSecOps to support its key principles and goals. Here's",
            "isTitleSlide": false,
            "isSectionDivider": false,
            "rawHtml": "<h3>© 2020  Cisco and/or its affiliates. All rights reserved.   Cisco Confidential</h3><p class=\"lead-statement\">The CALMS framework can be effectively applied to DevSecOps to support its key principles and goals. Here&#x27;s</p><div class=\"info-card mt-3\"><p>how each component, along with ―shift left‖ and ―shift right,‖ supports DevSecOps: Proactive, Shift-Left Approach This means applying proactive service management principles to the software delivery lifecycle - in other words, prevention. Reactive, Shift-Right Approach Reactive shift-right is about applying service delivery principles to service management. This is about using agile detection and correction.</p></div>",
